Generate a complete, self-contained Terraform repository for an ECS Fargate service behind an Application Load Balancer, deployed into an EXISTING VPC and existing subnets — do not create a VPC, subnets, NAT gateway, or internet gateway.

SPECS:
  output directory: {workspace}
  project/environment prefix: {project_name}
  AWS region: {aws_region}
  existing VPC id: {vpc_id}
  existing subnet ids: {subnet_ids}
  container image: {container_image}
  container port: {container_port}
  desired task count: {desired_count}
  task cpu,memory: {cpu_memory}

Emit these files, each as its own path-bearing fence rooted at {workspace}/:
  versions.tf       — terraform block, required_providers (hashicorp/aws, pinned major version), required_version
  variables.tf       — one variable per SPEC above (subnet_ids as list(string)), with type and description, no hardcoded defaults for anything SPEC-supplied
  main.tf            — aws_ecs_cluster, aws_ecs_task_definition (Fargate, awsvpc network mode, container definition built from container_image/container_port via jsonencode), aws_iam_role + aws_iam_role_policy_attachment for the task execution role (AmazonECSTaskExecutionRolePolicy), aws_security_group for the ECS tasks (ingress from the ALB security group only, on container_port), aws_security_group for the ALB (ingress 80 from 0.0.0.0/0), aws_lb, aws_lb_target_group (target_type = ip, health check on /), aws_lb_listener (port 80 forwarding to the target group), aws_ecs_service (Fargate launch type, network_configuration using the supplied subnet_ids and the task security group, load_balancer block wired to the target group, depends_on the listener), aws_cloudwatch_log_group for the task's awslogs driver
  outputs.tf         — cluster name, service name, ALB DNS name, log group name
  terraform.tfvars.example — one line per variable with a realistic placeholder value, no real secrets
  README.md          — what this deploys, prerequisites (AWS credentials, an existing VPC with the subnets already routed appropriately — public for the ALB, private-with-NAT or public for the tasks depending on the subnets supplied), and the exact terraform init/plan/apply commands to run from {workspace}

Every resource name must incorporate {project_name} so this repo is safely deployable alongside others in the same account/VPC. Do not invent variables not listed in SPECS without also adding them to variables.tf with a sensible default. Do not include a provider "aws" block with a hardcoded profile or access key — region only, sourced from the aws_region variable.

After the files, include ONE pathless bash fence that does exactly:
cd {workspace} && terraform init -backend=false && terraform validate
No other commentary outside the fences.
